          "significance": "CFTC Ethereum futures positioning provides a structured view of institutional, leveraged, dealer, and other trader exposure to Ethereum through regulated futures markets. Changes in open interest reveal changes in futures-market participation, while changes in long and short positions show how each trader group is adjusting exposure to Ethereum. Because Ethereum is a major cryptoasset with substantial derivatives activity, futures positioning can provide context for Ethereum market structure, institutional participation, derivatives-market sentiment, risk appetite, and changes in exposure to the broader crypto market.",
